name propbank-frames
# A frame file. A predicate is its lemma; a roleset is its predicate's lemma and the name PropBank writes for it
# ([abandon, leave behind]), the type the highway lists from these files, as a frame element is its frame and its
# name; its id (abandon.01) is the key PropBank and the resources that point at it write. A role's links name a
# VerbNet class or a FrameNet frame as those resources write them: each is read as that type. An example is its text;
# what is marked in it speaks of it. A part that is no thing (a role, a link, an alias) speaks of the nearest thing it
# is inside: the roleset.
match *.xml
format xml

thing predicate lemma
thing roleset ^predicate/lemma name
thing example text
key roleset id
type class vnclass fnframe
content lemma name pos descr f n resource rolelink alias type text arg rel slots slot head dep
# bookkeeping, read by nothing: which releases a roleset is in use in, a link's version, confidence and how it was made
omit usagenotes version confidence src start end relloc note

# What each part a claim is made of means (Laplace-Engine#32), in the words of PropBank's frameset.dtd, never an
# element's or an attribute's name:
# frameset.dtd: "Each predicate will contain a set of roles in an entity called a roleset. ... Multiple rolesets per
# predicate are necessary for the accomodation of different senses of the predicate."
relation "sense" predicate.roleset
# frameset.dtd: "pos = Part of Speech / Can take the following values: r = Adverb, p = Preposition, v = Verb, n = Noun,
# j = Adjective ...": an alias's pos is a value of PropBank's part-of-speech list, said of the roleset: [roleset, v]
value - alias.pos
# frameset.dtd: "roles have a number (or an "M" associated with them, for common adjuncts that don't qualify for
# number argument status). Both numbered arguments and adjuncts are labeled with the function tags from the list
# below: EXT extent, LOC location, ... PAG prototypical agent, PPT prototypical patient, ..." (an example's arg: "the n
# and f attributes corresponds to those of the roles described above")
relation "number" role.n
value - f
# frameset.dtd: "The rolesets give mneumonics of the argument labels for each different set of arguments."
relation "mneumonic" role.descr
# frameset.dtd: "The examples usually have names which are often space delimited descriptions of the annotation."
relation "description of the annotation" example.name
# frameset.dtd: "The examples contain plain text sentences and then assign arguments to segments of the sentence."
# An arg's type (ARG0, ARGM-TMP, ...: the DTD's list) is a value of PropBank's argument labels, the relation of the
# example to the segment it is assigned to: [example, ARG0, the Big Board].
value - arg.type
# frameset.dtd: "examples demonstrating some of the primary considerations in predicate argument annotation for the
# predicate+roleset in consideration": rel is the example's predicate, [example, predicate, abandoned]
relation "predicate" rel
# A link's class is the VerbNet class or FrameNet frame it names, read as that type (type class): a value of that
# road class, [roleset, leave-51.2]. Its resource (VerbNet, FrameNet) is which road class that is, said by the type the
# class is read as: no claim of its own (it stays content of the roleset's tree).
value - class
# An alias is a word PropBank lists for the roleset, a lemma (the DTD names it only: "<!ELEMENT alias (#PCDATA)>",
# with its "pos = Part of Speech"): a value, [roleset, abandonment]. A rolelink's text is the role the roleset's role is
# in the class it links to (theme, initial_location: VerbNet's thematic roles and FrameNet's frame elements, as PropBank
# writes them; the DTD names it only, "<!ELEMENT rolelink (#PCDATA)>"): a value of that resource's role inventory.
value - alias rolelink

holds predicate roleset
attest alias pos .
attest role descr f n
attest rolelink class .
attest lexlink class
attest example name
attest arg f
relate arg type to arg
attest rel .

# the highway: rolesets by their ids, and the VerbNet classes and FrameNet frames their links name
types pbroleset "PropBank roleset" roleset
keyed pbroleset roleset id
when resource is VerbNet
maps rolelink ^roleset/id pbroleset to class vnclass
maps lexlink ^roleset/id pbroleset to class vnclass
always
when resource is FrameNet
maps rolelink ^roleset/id pbroleset to class fnframe
maps lexlink ^roleset/id pbroleset to class fnframe
